    "result": "I implemented `plan_extraction` in `solution.py` and wrote 71 tests in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes. The implementation follows the spec: `dest` is validated and its trailing slashes stripped, `\\` and `/` are both treated as separators, `.` and empty segments are dropped, and `..` pops a segment or raises if it would climb above the destination. Members that are absolute, have a NUL, start with a drive prefix, or normalise to nothing raise `UnsafePathError`. Directory entries are validated but left out of the result. Case-insensitive duplicates raise, and the whole plan is built before anything is returned, so there is never a partial result. One test failed on the first run because I had written it wrongly: `a:b` is a drive prefix under the spec, so the code was right and I fixed the test. I could not run the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit gates from here, because only the test command is allowed. The helper functions are small, so complexity should be well under 10, but those gates are unverified.",
